# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[oc]
build/
dist/
wheels/
*.egg-info
.venv/

# Secrets
.env

# Long-term agent memory: facts a user stated about themselves. Personal data,
# never committed — data/ is otherwise tracked, so this rule must exist.
# Phase 6: one file per user under data/memory/; the old single file stays
# listed in case a copy is left behind.
data/memory/
data/user_memory.json

# Front end
web/node_modules/
web/dist/

# One-off diagnostics and console leftovers
src/_diag*.py
q.json
toc_*.txt

# Translation round-trip: the script is kept, its intermediate files are not
tools/comments.json
tools/comments.en.json

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Data. Order matters: the LAST matching rule wins in git, so
# exclusions come first and anything worth keeping comes after.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Regenerated by the scripts, and large
data/raw/
data/meta/
data/vectors.npy
data/chunks.jsonl

# Working state and caches
data/embed_state.json
data/chunk_ids.json
data/llm_expand_cache.json

# Everything else under data/ is measurement results, and that is the value:
# the golden set, the synonym dictionary, the manifest holding the core
# selection rule, the reports for every configuration, the manual annotation.
# None of it is reproducible automatically.
